# Animation libraries

Motion (`motion/react`) owns entrance and hover: opacity and a 16–24px move, about 450–700ms, played once.

Anime.js v4 (`animejs`) owns SVG stroke drawing, arrowheads, and number counts. Import `animate`, `createTimeline`, and `svg` from `animejs`. Draw with `svg.createDrawable()` and `draw: ['0 0', '0 1']`. Update object values in `onRender`.

Never animate the same property on the same element with both libraries.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — both libraries animate opacity on the card
animate(card, { opacity: [0, 1] });
<motion.article animate={{ opacity: 1 }} />

// ✅ GOOD — Motion moves the card; Anime.js draws the connector
<motion.article initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 18 }} whileInView={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }} />
animate(svg.createDrawable(path)[0], { draw: ['0 0', '0 1'], duration: 620 });
```

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` by showing the finished state immediately. Cancel anime instances and disconnect observers on unmount.
